.TH GIT-AUTOCOMMIT 1 "August 2026" "git-autocommit 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-autocommit \- split staged changes into reviewed atomic Conventional Commits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git autocommit
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B git-autocommit
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-autocommit
uses an OpenAI-compatible model to propose commit messages and group whole staged files into atomic Conventional Commits.
The proposed plan is validated before repository mutation: every staged path must appear exactly once, invented paths are rejected, and the generated commit chain must reproduce the captured staged tree.
.PP
Interactive review is enabled by default. After deterministic validation, the command displays the complete plan and requires an explicit commit, retry, or abort decision. Retry requests an alternative valid plan against the same captured staged snapshot. Non-interactive callers must explicitly disable review.
.PP
The command captures
.B HEAD
and the staged tree before contacting the model. Before retrying or moving
.BR HEAD ,
it verifies that neither has changed. Generated commits are signed by default. Normal Git commit hooks are not run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --base-url " URL"
Override the OpenAI-compatible API base URL.
.TP
.BI --model " MODEL"
Override the model name.
.TP
.BI --timeout " SECONDS"
Override the HTTP timeout. The value must be positive.
.TP
.BI --prompt-dir " PATH"
Load custom
.I system.md
and
.I plan.md
prompt files from another directory.
.TP
.B --single
Require exactly one commit containing every staged path.
.TP
.B --no-single
Disable single-commit mode configured through TOML or the environment.
.TP
.B --sign
Enable commit signing, overriding lower-precedence configuration.
.TP
.B --no-sign
Disable commit signing, overriding lower-precedence configuration.
.TP
.B --review
Require interactive review before committing. This is the default.
.TP
.B --no-review
Explicitly allow a validated plan to commit without interactive review. Intended for trusted unattended callers.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Contact the model, validate the plan, and print it without prompting, creating commits, or moving
.BR HEAD .
.TP
.B --show-prompt
Render prompts from staged content and exit without contacting the model.
.TP
.B --show-config
Print resolved configuration, including review policy, and exit before reading staged changes.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help information.
.SH INTERACTIVE REVIEW
After a plan passes deterministic validation, review presents:
.PP
.nf
[c] commit  [r] retry  [a] abort
> 
.fi
.PP
Pressing Enter alone does not approve the plan.
.B c
commits the displayed plan,
.B r
rejects it and requests an alternative plan for the same captured staged snapshot, and
.B a
exits without repository mutation.
.PP
Each explicit retry sends the staged planning context to the configured model endpoint again. Before a retry and before commit, the command verifies that
.B HEAD
and the staged tree still match the captured snapshot.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Repository configuration is read from
.IR .git/autocommit.toml .
Precedence is command-line options, environment variables, repository configuration, then built-in defaults.
.PP
Supported TOML keys are
.BR base_url ,
.BR model ,
.BR timeout_seconds ,
.BR prompt_dir ,
.BR max_diff_bytes ,
.BR max_prompt_bytes ,
.BR max_commits ,
.BR single_commit ,
.BR sign_commits ,
and
.BR review_before_commit .
.PP
Supported environment variables are
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_BASE_URL ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_MODEL ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_TIMEOUT ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_PROMPT_DIR ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_MAX_DIFF_BYTES ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_MAX_COMMITS ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_SINGLE_COMMIT ,
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_SIGN_COMMITS ,
and
.BR GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_REVIEW .
.PP
Review defaults to enabled. Set
.B review_before_commit = false
or
.B GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_REVIEW=false
for a persistent explicit unattended policy, or use
.B --no-review
for one invocation.
.PP
The legacy
.B DUBNIUM_LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL
and
.B DUBNIUM_LOCAL_LLM_MODEL
variables are accepted as fallback aliases.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .git/autocommit.toml
Per-repository configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/git-autocommit/system.md
Default location for an optional custom system prompt.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/git-autocommit/plan.md
Default location for an optional custom plan prompt.
.SH SECURITY
Staged path names, diff statistics, and bounded staged diff content are sent to the configured model endpoint. Review that endpoint's transport, access, retention, and training policies before using it with sensitive repositories. Human retries resend that staged context.
.PP
Interactive review fails closed unless standard input is interactive and standard output is attached to a terminal so the approved plan is visible. Unattended callers must explicitly opt out with
.BR --no-review ,
.B GIT_AUTOCOMMIT_REVIEW=false,
or
.B review_before_commit = false.
.PP
Normal commit hooks are intentionally not run. Run required formatting, tests, secret scanning, DCO checks, and other policy gates before invoking the command, or enforce them in CI.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create reviewed commits using the defaults:
.PP
.nf
git add src/ tests/
git autocommit
.fi
.PP
Preview a validated plan without changing the repository:
.PP
.nf
git autocommit --dry-run
.fi
.PP
Run explicitly without interactive review or signing:
.PP
.nf
git autocommit --no-review --no-sign
.fi
.PP
Inspect resolved configuration:
.PP
.nf
git autocommit --show-config
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and non-zero when configuration, model communication, plan validation, review preconditions, Git operations, signing, or concurrency checks fail.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-commit (1),
.BR git-add (1)
